{"additions":216,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n- The help overlay's \"Switch view\" row is generated from the `app { }` keymap (`AppContext::page_keys`, computed in `App::new`) instead of being hard-coded per page — a user rebinding `\"w\" \"page:worktrees\"` now shows `w`. Header tab numbers stay **positional** (a page's slot); making slots explicit in the config is tracked in #114.\n- Worktrees stash preview: `stash_patch` only retries without `--include-untracked` when git rejects the option; the file list is one shared `Rc<Vec<FileDiff>>` instead of a clone.\n\nAddresses the remaining Copilot threads on #110.\n\n## Changes\n- `Keymap::entries()`; `page_keys()` + `AppContext::page_keys`; `App::active_help_bindings()` prepends the generated entry; hard-coded entries removed from every page's `help_bindings()`; CLAUDE.md checklist updated\n- `worktrees::domain::stash`: `include_untracked_unsupported` decision + test\n- `worktrees::panes::preview`: `Rc` sharing between `Content::Stash` and the diff widget\n\n## Not verified\n- Demo GIFs are not re-recorded here; they will be re-recorded once the Actions page (#112) is merged so all tabs are present.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":13,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T09:01:36Z","deletions":46,"headRefName":"fix/page-keys-and-stash","labels":[],"number":113,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPqrvQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe changes are cohesive and low-risk, with updated tests and only minor optional nits around unnecessary `pub` visibility.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR refines view-switch UX by deriving page-switch key labels from the `app { }` keymap (for both header tabs and the Help overlay), and improves the Worktrees stash preview path by tightening the `--include-untracked` fallback behavior and avoiding an unnecessary `Vec<FileDiff>` clone via `Rc`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Derive per-page switch-key display strings from the app keymap insertion order and use them in the header and Help overlay.\n- Remove per-page hardcoded “Switch view” help entries and adjust related tests to assert the new behavior.\n- Fix stash preview internals: conditional fallback when `--include-untracked` is unsupported; share diff file lists with `Rc<Vec<FileDiff>>`.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/core/keymap.rs | Adds `Keymap::entries()` to expose bindings in insertion order for downstream derivations. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Computes/stores `AppContext::page_keys` in `App::new`; prepends unified “Switch view” help entry via `active_help_bindings()`. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Updates tab rendering to show `<first page key>:<label>` (or just `<label>` if unbound). |\r\n| src/git/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry from Git page help bindings. |\r\n| src/github/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry from GitHub page help bindings. |\r\n| src/files/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry from Files page help bindings. |\r\n| src/docker/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry and updates tests to assert absence of “Switch view” in page-local help. |\r\n| src/procs/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry; updates tests and `AppContext` construction to include `page_keys`. |\r\n| src/worktrees/state.rs | Removes hardcoded view-switch help entry from Worktrees page help bindings. |\r\n| src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs | Restricts `--include-untracked` retry to “unsupported option” errors; adds helper + unit test. |\r\n| src/worktrees/panes/preview.rs | Shares stash diff file list via a single `Rc<Vec<FileDiff>>` between content and diff widget. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Initializes new `AppContext::page_keys` field during TUI startup. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates “How to add a page” guidance to reflect centralized view-switch help/header derivation. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 13/13 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:05:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b45fa2b98cba6d4930ab392d1084c1e906bdbe4f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPsNXw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:08:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b45fa2b98cba6d4930ab392d1084c1e906bdbe4f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPsOTA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:08:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"bef7b653a617b6f5ee21ed2b0f1456e14c0af079"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPt_1Q","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe new `include_untracked_unsupported()` helper is overly permissive (it can match unrelated “unknown option” errors), which can incorrectly trigger the fallback retry behavior.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs:106**\n* `include_untracked_unsupported` is currently too permissive: it returns true for any stderr containing \"unknown option\" even if the message doesn’t mention `include-untracked`, which can cause an unnecessary retry on unrelated failures. Since this helper is specifically about `--include-untracked`, it should require that the message mentions `include-untracked` and indicates an unknown/unrecognized option/switch.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 170 of the same file.\n```\nfn include_untracked_unsupported(stderr: &str) -> bool {\n    let text = stderr.to_ascii_lowercase();\n    text.contains(\"unknown option\") || text.contains(\"include-untracked\")\n}\n```\n\n**src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs:170**\n* This test case asserts that an arbitrary \"unknown option `u`\" error should trigger the `--include-untracked` fallback, but after tightening the helper to only match errors that actually mention `include-untracked`, this should be a negative case (otherwise it encourages overly broad matching).\n```\n        assert!(include_untracked_unsupported(\"unknown option `u'\"));\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 13/13 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:11:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"bef7b653a617b6f5ee21ed2b0f1456e14c0af079"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPxc8A","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new stash fallback predicate can incorrectly classify non-`--include-untracked` failures (and tests/comments reflect that), so it should be tightened and aligned before merge.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs:106**\n* `include_untracked_unsupported` currently returns true for any \"unknown option\" error, even if the error is unrelated to `--include-untracked`. That can trigger a retry and potentially mask the real failure. Tighten the predicate to require that the message mentions `include-untracked` as well.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 170 of the same file.\n```\nfn include_untracked_unsupported(stderr: &str) -> bool {\n    let text = stderr.to_ascii_lowercase();\n    text.contains(\"unknown option\") || text.contains(\"include-untracked\")\n}\n```\n\n**src/worktrees/domain/stash.rs:170**\n* This assertion contradicts the test name (it accepts an unrelated unknown-option error). If the fallback is meant to be specific to `--include-untracked`, this should be false.\n```\n        assert!(include_untracked_unsupported(\"unknown option `u'\"));\n```\n**src/core/app.rs:414**\n* The header shows slot numbers (tab position), not keys; unbinding `7` should only affect the help \"Switch view\" entry (and `page_keys`), not the header.\n```\n        // Unbinding the built-in key leaves only the user's key, so the\n        // header shows `w:Worktrees`.\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 13/13 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:18:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cc20eba2df0ec8ff14a111a2bbd28c4a11c46a17"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLZzmNQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nIt leaves demo GIFs stale despite changing help-overlay output, and it contains incorrect test comments about header numbering vs key bindings that should be corrected.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/core/app.rs:376**\n* The help overlay’s “Switch view” row is derived from the `app { }` keymap, but header tab numbers are still positional (slot index). This test doc comment currently states that header tab labels are derived from the `app { }` block and that a page bound to `7` shows `7` instead of its position, which contradicts `status_bar.rs` and the PR description.\n```\n    /// The header tab labels and the help \"Switch view\" entry are derived\n    /// from the `app { }` block, so a page bound to `7` shows `7`, not its\n    /// position (`6`).\n```\n**src/core/app.rs:422**\n* This comment says unbinding `7` makes the header show `w:Worktrees`, but the header tab number is the page slot (position), not the bound key. Only the help overlay’s “Switch view” entry should change when rebinding/unbinding keys.\n```\n        // Unbinding the built-in key leaves only the user's key, so the\n        // header shows `w:Worktrees`.\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 13/13 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-30T07:29:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"337271bac30dce76b04490424e40f3fd65b0cff4"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:19Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299281800/job/99224250732","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:29Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:22Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194099/job/99224005148","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:09Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:42Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194068/job/99224005017","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:08Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:18Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194099/job/99224005151","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:10Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:55Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194099/job/99224005030","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:55Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194099/job/99224193928","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:55Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:19Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299281800/job/99224235755","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:19Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:52Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194068/job/99224005098","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:08Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:27:02Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299194068/job/99224005109","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:26:08Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:19Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299281800/job/99224236009","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:28:20Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"♻️ Derive the view-switch help from the app keymap; stash preview fixes"}
